{"authored" [{"question" "e-473" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac{1}{\\sin x}\\left(\\cot x + \\sin^2 x\\right)\\,\\textrm d x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/example-473.json" "file_sha256" "19565420ea91fdf3f885b86ce6b8981d9a672c9823b1af7837075aafda7ee4ef" "basis" 1121 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-473" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We multiply out the parentheses and then use the identity $\\dfrac{1}{\\sin x } = \\csc x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}(\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot \\operatorname{cot}⁡x+\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot {sin}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{cot}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/example-473.json" "file_sha256" "19565420ea91fdf3f885b86ce6b8981d9a672c9823b1af7837075aafda7ee4ef" "basis" 1121 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-474" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int_0^{\\pi/3} \\dfrac{\\sin x}{\\cos^2 x}\\,\\textrm d x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/example-474.json" "file_sha256" "2cf8fdba454e5efb27b58c622b730f477ce82ca1ad68f95457734834988305c4" "basis" 1121 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-474" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int_0^{\\pi/3} \\dfrac{\\sin x}{\\cos^2 x}\\,\\textrm d x =  \\int_0^{\\pi/3} \\dfrac{1}{\\cos x}\\cdot \\dfrac{\\sin x}{\\cos x}\\,\\textrm d x.\n$$\n\nWe then use the fact that $\\dfrac{\\sin x }{\\cos x}  = \\tan x$ and $\\dfrac{1}{\\cos x} = \\sec x$ to express this as\n\n$$\n\\int_0^{\\pi/3} \\sec x\\tan x\\,\\textrm d x,\n$$\n\nwhich is a standard trigonometric integral. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡x{|}_{0}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})-\\operatorname{sec}⁡(0) \\\\  & =2-1 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/example-474.json" "file_sha256" "2cf8fdba454e5efb27b58c622b730f477ce82ca1ad68f95457734834988305c4" "basis" 1121 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-475" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int \\tan{2x}\\,\\textrm d x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/example-475.json" "file_sha256" "5e7ecb49eb8ea90acd2d7b3ccea5aa4987a0f40cd782d7721fbf5aa823b7c197" "basis" 1121 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-475" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We use the identity $\\tan 2x = \\dfrac{\\sin 2x}{\\cos 2x}$ and rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\tan{2x}\\,\\textrm d x = \\int \\dfrac{\\sin{2x}}{\\cos 2x}\\,\\textrm d x.\n$$\n\nNotice that the numerator of the integrand is proportional to the derivative of the denominator. So, we can solve this by substitution.\n\nLet $u=\\cos 2x.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}=-2 \\sin 2x \\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad -\\dfrac 1 2 \\,\\textrm d u= \\sin 2x \\, \\textrm d x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x|+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)^{-1}|+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{sec}⁡2x|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/example-475.json" "file_sha256" "5e7ecb49eb8ea90acd2d7b3ccea5aa4987a0f40cd782d7721fbf5aa823b7c197" "basis" 1121 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006925/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-352868" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /12}\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038169/state.json" "file_sha256" "17374b52377599dede2a15c883d45326524032b972d8cc29a2ff0e5d5334ad8c" "basis" 1296 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038169/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-352868" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We can rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /12}\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /12}\\operatorname{tan}⁡4x\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThen, we use the fact that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡4x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}$ and $\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡4x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /12}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /12}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this by substitution. Let $u=4x.$ Then $\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{4}\\text{d}u.$\n\nNow, we fill the table for the limits of integration, according to the rule $u=4x.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{12}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ |\n\nTherefore, the integral in terms of the new variable is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /12}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡u{|}_{0}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}(cos\\,(\\frac{\\pi }{3})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}(\\frac{1}{2}-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038169/state.json" "file_sha256" "17374b52377599dede2a15c883d45326524032b972d8cc29a2ff0e5d5334ad8c" "basis" 1296 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038169/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-352868" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038169/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ce191542b27f7f51d6b6ef778426f64d00c2b3bdc3edfb369c14f54dac6911a4" "basis" 1296 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038169/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-352868" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038169/state.json" "file_sha256" "17374b52377599dede2a15c883d45326524032b972d8cc29a2ff0e5d5334ad8c" "basis" 1296 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038169/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-352868" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{8}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038169/state.json" "file_sha256" "17374b52377599dede2a15c883d45326524032b972d8cc29a2ff0e5d5334ad8c" "basis" 1296 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038169/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-49274" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/state.json" "file_sha256" "e00ad799e0b97bfb1d4d638c8915886f8acb46041a26f2fcec39115b86c604f7"} {"question" "q-49274" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We use the identity $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/state.json" "file_sha256" "e00ad799e0b97bfb1d4d638c8915886f8acb46041a26f2fcec39115b86c604f7"} {"question" "q-49274" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "546f1f13e6c6245ead185c28e301f1b73c953ef685d98e2a802fcaeb48a313f2"} {"question" "q-49274" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/state.json" "file_sha256" "e00ad799e0b97bfb1d4d638c8915886f8acb46041a26f2fcec39115b86c604f7"} {"question" "q-49274" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C"] ["math" "-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/state.json" "file_sha256" "e00ad799e0b97bfb1d4d638c8915886f8acb46041a26f2fcec39115b86c604f7"} {"question" "q-49274" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/state.json" "file_sha256" "e00ad799e0b97bfb1d4d638c8915886f8acb46041a26f2fcec39115b86c604f7"} {"question" "q-49070" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\operatorname{tan}⁡x(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/state.json" "file_sha256" "e00ad799e0b97bfb1d4d638c8915886f8acb46041a26f2fcec39115b86c604f7"} {"question" "q-49070" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We multiply out the parentheses and then use the identity $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{tan}⁡x(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\cdot 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cdot 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x+2\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/state.json" "file_sha256" "e00ad799e0b97bfb1d4d638c8915886f8acb46041a26f2fcec39115b86c604f7"} {"question" "q-49070" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "546f1f13e6c6245ead185c28e301f1b73c953ef685d98e2a802fcaeb48a313f2"} {"question" "q-49070" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/state.json" "file_sha256" "e00ad799e0b97bfb1d4d638c8915886f8acb46041a26f2fcec39115b86c604f7"} {"question" "q-49070" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/state.json" "file_sha256" "e00ad799e0b97bfb1d4d638c8915886f8acb46041a26f2fcec39115b86c604f7"} {"question" "q-49070" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/state.json" "file_sha256" "e00ad799e0b97bfb1d4d638c8915886f8acb46041a26f2fcec39115b86c604f7"} {"question" "q-49272" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\operatorname{cot}⁡x(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/state.json" "file_sha256" "e00ad799e0b97bfb1d4d638c8915886f8acb46041a26f2fcec39115b86c604f7"} {"question" "q-49272" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We multiply out the parentheses and then use the identities $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x},$ and $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{cot}⁡x(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-x+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/state.json" "file_sha256" "e00ad799e0b97bfb1d4d638c8915886f8acb46041a26f2fcec39115b86c604f7"} {"question" "q-49272" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "546f1f13e6c6245ead185c28e301f1b73c953ef685d98e2a802fcaeb48a313f2"} {"question" "q-49272" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/state.json" "file_sha256" "e00ad799e0b97bfb1d4d638c8915886f8acb46041a26f2fcec39115b86c604f7"} {"question" "q-49272" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-x+C"] ["math" "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-x+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-x+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-x+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/state.json" "file_sha256" "e00ad799e0b97bfb1d4d638c8915886f8acb46041a26f2fcec39115b86c604f7"} {"question" "q-49272" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-x+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/state.json" "file_sha256" "e00ad799e0b97bfb1d4d638c8915886f8acb46041a26f2fcec39115b86c604f7"} {"question" "q-51109" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/state.json" "file_sha256" "e00ad799e0b97bfb1d4d638c8915886f8acb46041a26f2fcec39115b86c604f7"} {"question" "q-51109" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We use the identity $\\operatorname{tan}⁡2x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this by substitution. Let $u=2x.$ Then $\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u.$ \n\nNow, we fill the table for the limits of integration, according to the rule $u=2x.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ |\n\nTherefore, the integral in terms of the new variable is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡u}{2}{|}_{0}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/state.json" "file_sha256" "e00ad799e0b97bfb1d4d638c8915886f8acb46041a26f2fcec39115b86c604f7"} {"question" "q-51109" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "546f1f13e6c6245ead185c28e301f1b73c953ef685d98e2a802fcaeb48a313f2"} {"question" "q-51109" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/state.json" "file_sha256" "e00ad799e0b97bfb1d4d638c8915886f8acb46041a26f2fcec39115b86c604f7"} {"question" "q-51109" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/state.json" "file_sha256" "e00ad799e0b97bfb1d4d638c8915886f8acb46041a26f2fcec39115b86c604f7"} {"question" "q-51109" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{4}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/state.json" "file_sha256" "e00ad799e0b97bfb1d4d638c8915886f8acb46041a26f2fcec39115b86c604f7"} {"question" "q-49258" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{4}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/state.json" "file_sha256" "e00ad799e0b97bfb1d4d638c8915886f8acb46041a26f2fcec39115b86c604f7"} {"question" "q-49258" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We use the identity $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{4}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/state.json" "file_sha256" "e00ad799e0b97bfb1d4d638c8915886f8acb46041a26f2fcec39115b86c604f7"} {"question" "q-49258" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "546f1f13e6c6245ead185c28e301f1b73c953ef685d98e2a802fcaeb48a313f2"} {"question" "q-49258" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/state.json" "file_sha256" "e00ad799e0b97bfb1d4d638c8915886f8acb46041a26f2fcec39115b86c604f7"} {"question" "q-49258" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/state.json" "file_sha256" "e00ad799e0b97bfb1d4d638c8915886f8acb46041a26f2fcec39115b86c604f7"} {"question" "q-49258" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/state.json" "file_sha256" "e00ad799e0b97bfb1d4d638c8915886f8acb46041a26f2fcec39115b86c604f7"} {"question" "q-352853" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{1+\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/state.json" "file_sha256" "e00ad799e0b97bfb1d4d638c8915886f8acb46041a26f2fcec39115b86c604f7"} {"question" "q-352853" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We use the identities $\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$  and  $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{1+\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}\\cdot (1+\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x(1+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x){|}_{0}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}-\\frac{1}{2})-(0-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/state.json" "file_sha256" "e00ad799e0b97bfb1d4d638c8915886f8acb46041a26f2fcec39115b86c604f7"} {"question" "q-352853" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "546f1f13e6c6245ead185c28e301f1b73c953ef685d98e2a802fcaeb48a313f2"} {"question" "q-352853" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/state.json" "file_sha256" "e00ad799e0b97bfb1d4d638c8915886f8acb46041a26f2fcec39115b86c604f7"} {"question" "q-352853" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/state.json" "file_sha256" "e00ad799e0b97bfb1d4d638c8915886f8acb46041a26f2fcec39115b86c604f7"} {"question" "q-352868" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /12}\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/state.json" "file_sha256" "e00ad799e0b97bfb1d4d638c8915886f8acb46041a26f2fcec39115b86c604f7"} {"question" "q-352868" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We can rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /12}\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /12}\\operatorname{tan}⁡4x\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThen, we use the fact that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡4x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}$ and $\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡4x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /12}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /12}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this by substitution. Let $u=4x.$ Then $\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{4}\\text{d}u.$\n\nNow, we fill the table for the limits of integration, according to the rule $u=4x.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{12}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ |\n\nTherefore, the integral in terms of the new variable is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /12}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡u{|}_{0}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}(cos\\,(\\frac{\\pi }{3})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}(\\frac{1}{2}-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/state.json" "file_sha256" "e00ad799e0b97bfb1d4d638c8915886f8acb46041a26f2fcec39115b86c604f7"} {"question" "q-352868" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "546f1f13e6c6245ead185c28e301f1b73c953ef685d98e2a802fcaeb48a313f2"} {"question" "q-352868" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/state.json" "file_sha256" "e00ad799e0b97bfb1d4d638c8915886f8acb46041a26f2fcec39115b86c604f7"} {"question" "q-352868" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{8}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/state.json" "file_sha256" "e00ad799e0b97bfb1d4d638c8915886f8acb46041a26f2fcec39115b86c604f7"} {"question" "q-114313" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/state.json" "file_sha256" "e00ad799e0b97bfb1d4d638c8915886f8acb46041a26f2fcec39115b86c604f7"} {"question" "q-114313" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x)\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe then use the fact that $\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}=\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}$ to express this as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{cot}⁡x(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x)\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{csc}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{csc}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x)\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-(-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x)+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/state.json" "file_sha256" "e00ad799e0b97bfb1d4d638c8915886f8acb46041a26f2fcec39115b86c604f7"} {"question" "q-114313" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "546f1f13e6c6245ead185c28e301f1b73c953ef685d98e2a802fcaeb48a313f2"} {"question" "q-114313" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/state.json" "file_sha256" "e00ad799e0b97bfb1d4d638c8915886f8acb46041a26f2fcec39115b86c604f7"} {"question" "q-114313" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{csc}⁡x-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/state.json" "file_sha256" "e00ad799e0b97bfb1d4d638c8915886f8acb46041a26f2fcec39115b86c604f7"} {"question" "q-114313" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/state.json" "file_sha256" "e00ad799e0b97bfb1d4d638c8915886f8acb46041a26f2fcec39115b86c604f7"} {"question" "q-73361" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate ${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{1+\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/state.json" "file_sha256" "e00ad799e0b97bfb1d4d638c8915886f8acb46041a26f2fcec39115b86c604f7"} {"question" "q-73361" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We can write the integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{1+\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}\\text{d}x={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}\\cdot (1+\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nWe then use the fact that $\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x$ and $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}\\cdot (1+\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot (1+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x){|}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & (\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}))-(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})-(0-1) \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/state.json" "file_sha256" "e00ad799e0b97bfb1d4d638c8915886f8acb46041a26f2fcec39115b86c604f7"} {"question" "q-73361" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "546f1f13e6c6245ead185c28e301f1b73c953ef685d98e2a802fcaeb48a313f2"} {"question" "q-73361" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/state.json" "file_sha256" "e00ad799e0b97bfb1d4d638c8915886f8acb46041a26f2fcec39115b86c604f7"} {"question" "q-73361" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{2}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{2}-2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/state.json" "file_sha256" "e00ad799e0b97bfb1d4d638c8915886f8acb46041a26f2fcec39115b86c604f7"} {"question" "q-73361" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/state.json" "file_sha256" "e00ad799e0b97bfb1d4d638c8915886f8acb46041a26f2fcec39115b86c604f7"} {"question" "q-114306" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{3\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/state.json" "file_sha256" "e00ad799e0b97bfb1d4d638c8915886f8acb46041a26f2fcec39115b86c604f7"} {"question" "q-114306" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We can write the integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{3\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=3{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nThen, we use the fact that $\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =3{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{3\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =3{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =3[\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})-\\operatorname{sec}⁡0] \\\\  & =3(\\sqrt{2}-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/state.json" "file_sha256" "e00ad799e0b97bfb1d4d638c8915886f8acb46041a26f2fcec39115b86c604f7"} {"question" "q-114306" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "546f1f13e6c6245ead185c28e301f1b73c953ef685d98e2a802fcaeb48a313f2"} {"question" "q-114306" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/state.json" "file_sha256" "e00ad799e0b97bfb1d4d638c8915886f8acb46041a26f2fcec39115b86c604f7"} {"question" "q-114306" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3(\\sqrt{2}+1)"] ["math" "3(\\sqrt{2}-1)"] ["math" "3(\\sqrt{2}-2)"] ["math" "\\sqrt{2}+1"] ["math" "\\sqrt{2}-3"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/state.json" "file_sha256" "e00ad799e0b97bfb1d4d638c8915886f8acb46041a26f2fcec39115b86c604f7"} {"question" "q-114306" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3(\\sqrt{2}-1)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/state.json" "file_sha256" "e00ad799e0b97bfb1d4d638c8915886f8acb46041a26f2fcec39115b86c604f7"} {"question" "q-49259" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/state.json" "file_sha256" "e00ad799e0b97bfb1d4d638c8915886f8acb46041a26f2fcec39115b86c604f7"} {"question" "q-49259" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We use the identity $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}$ and rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe can solve this by substitution. Let $u=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$ Then \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{sin}⁡x|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/state.json" "file_sha256" "e00ad799e0b97bfb1d4d638c8915886f8acb46041a26f2fcec39115b86c604f7"} {"question" "q-49259" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "546f1f13e6c6245ead185c28e301f1b73c953ef685d98e2a802fcaeb48a313f2"} {"question" "q-49259" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/state.json" "file_sha256" "e00ad799e0b97bfb1d4d638c8915886f8acb46041a26f2fcec39115b86c604f7"} {"question" "q-49259" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|)+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{csc}⁡x|+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{sin}⁡x|+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|)+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/state.json" "file_sha256" "e00ad799e0b97bfb1d4d638c8915886f8acb46041a26f2fcec39115b86c604f7"} {"question" "q-49259" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{sin}⁡x|+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/state.json" "file_sha256" "e00ad799e0b97bfb1d4d638c8915886f8acb46041a26f2fcec39115b86c604f7"} {"question" "q-49278" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡3x\\operatorname{sec}⁡3x\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/state.json" "file_sha256" "e00ad799e0b97bfb1d4d638c8915886f8acb46041a26f2fcec39115b86c604f7"} {"question" "q-49278" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We use the identity $\\operatorname{sec}⁡3x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x}$ and rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡3x\\operatorname{sec}⁡3x\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡3x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe can solve this by substitution. Let $u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x.$ Then \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x\\,⟹\\,-\\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡3x\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\frac{1}{3}\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x|+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|(\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x)^{-1}|+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{sec}⁡3x|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/state.json" "file_sha256" "e00ad799e0b97bfb1d4d638c8915886f8acb46041a26f2fcec39115b86c604f7"} {"question" "q-49278" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "546f1f13e6c6245ead185c28e301f1b73c953ef685d98e2a802fcaeb48a313f2"} {"question" "q-49278" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/state.json" "file_sha256" "e00ad799e0b97bfb1d4d638c8915886f8acb46041a26f2fcec39115b86c604f7"} {"question" "q-49278" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x|+C"] ["math" "3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x|+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x|+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{csc}⁡3x|+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{sec}⁡3x|+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/state.json" "file_sha256" "e00ad799e0b97bfb1d4d638c8915886f8acb46041a26f2fcec39115b86c604f7"} {"question" "q-49278" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{sec}⁡3x|+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/state.json" "file_sha256" "e00ad799e0b97bfb1d4d638c8915886f8acb46041a26f2fcec39115b86c604f7"} {"question" "q-49280" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/state.json" "file_sha256" "e00ad799e0b97bfb1d4d638c8915886f8acb46041a26f2fcec39115b86c604f7"} {"question" "q-49280" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\operatorname{tan}⁡4x\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe then use the fact that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡4x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}$ to express this as\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the identity $\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}=\\operatorname{sec}⁡4x$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {sec}^{2}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this by substitution. Let $u=4x.$ Then $\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{4}\\text{d}u.$ Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {sec}^{2}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {sec}^{2}⁡u\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\int {sec}^{2}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{tan}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{tan}⁡4x+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/state.json" "file_sha256" "e00ad799e0b97bfb1d4d638c8915886f8acb46041a26f2fcec39115b86c604f7"} {"question" "q-49280" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "546f1f13e6c6245ead185c28e301f1b73c953ef685d98e2a802fcaeb48a313f2"} {"question" "q-49280" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/state.json" "file_sha256" "e00ad799e0b97bfb1d4d638c8915886f8acb46041a26f2fcec39115b86c604f7"} {"question" "q-49280" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "4\\operatorname{tan}⁡4x+C"] ["math" "4\\operatorname{tan}⁡4x\\operatorname{sec}⁡4x+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{tan}⁡4x+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{tan}⁡4x\\operatorname{sec}⁡4x+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}{tan}^{2}⁡4x+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/state.json" "file_sha256" "e00ad799e0b97bfb1d4d638c8915886f8acb46041a26f2fcec39115b86c604f7"} {"question" "q-49280" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{tan}⁡4x+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/state.json" "file_sha256" "e00ad799e0b97bfb1d4d638c8915886f8acb46041a26f2fcec39115b86c604f7"} {"question" "q-352797" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /12}\\frac{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/state.json" "file_sha256" "e00ad799e0b97bfb1d4d638c8915886f8acb46041a26f2fcec39115b86c604f7"} {"question" "q-352797" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We can solve this by substitution. Let $u=1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x.$ Then \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNow, we fill the table for the limits of integration, according to the rule $u=1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{12}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $\\frac{3}{2}$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /12}\\frac{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{3/2}\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|{|}_{1}^{3/2} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{3}{2})-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{3}{2})\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/state.json" "file_sha256" "e00ad799e0b97bfb1d4d638c8915886f8acb46041a26f2fcec39115b86c604f7"} {"question" "q-352797" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "546f1f13e6c6245ead185c28e301f1b73c953ef685d98e2a802fcaeb48a313f2"} {"question" "q-352797" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/state.json" "file_sha256" "e00ad799e0b97bfb1d4d638c8915886f8acb46041a26f2fcec39115b86c604f7"} {"question" "q-352797" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\ln(\\frac{3}{2})"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/state.json" "file_sha256" "e00ad799e0b97bfb1d4d638c8915886f8acb46041a26f2fcec39115b86c604f7"} {"question" "q-352786" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}{sec}^{3}\\,x\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/state.json" "file_sha256" "e00ad799e0b97bfb1d4d638c8915886f8acb46041a26f2fcec39115b86c604f7"} {"question" "q-352786" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We can solve this by substitution. Let $u=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x.$ Then \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNow, we fill the table for the limits of integration, according to the rule $u=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}{sec}^{3}\\,x\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}{sec}^{2}\\,x\\cdot \\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{u}^{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{{u}^{3}}{3}{|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}({2}^{3}-{1}^{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(8-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{3}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/state.json" "file_sha256" "e00ad799e0b97bfb1d4d638c8915886f8acb46041a26f2fcec39115b86c604f7"} {"question" "q-352786" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "546f1f13e6c6245ead185c28e301f1b73c953ef685d98e2a802fcaeb48a313f2"} {"question" "q-352786" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/state.json" "file_sha256" "e00ad799e0b97bfb1d4d638c8915886f8acb46041a26f2fcec39115b86c604f7"} {"question" "q-352786" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{7}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/state.json" "file_sha256" "e00ad799e0b97bfb1d4d638c8915886f8acb46041a26f2fcec39115b86c604f7"} {"question" "e-473" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac{1}{\\sin x}\\left(\\cot x + \\sin^2 x\\right)\\,\\textrm d x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/example-473.json" "file_sha256" "19565420ea91fdf3f885b86ce6b8981d9a672c9823b1af7837075aafda7ee4ef"} {"question" "e-473" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We multiply out the parentheses and then use the identity $\\dfrac{1}{\\sin x } = \\csc x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}(\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot \\operatorname{cot}⁡x+\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot {sin}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{cot}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/example-473.json" "file_sha256" "19565420ea91fdf3f885b86ce6b8981d9a672c9823b1af7837075aafda7ee4ef"} {"question" "e-474" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int_0^{\\pi/3} \\dfrac{\\sin x}{\\cos^2 x}\\,\\textrm d x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/example-474.json" "file_sha256" "2cf8fdba454e5efb27b58c622b730f477ce82ca1ad68f95457734834988305c4"} {"question" "e-474" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int_0^{\\pi/3} \\dfrac{\\sin x}{\\cos^2 x}\\,\\textrm d x =  \\int_0^{\\pi/3} \\dfrac{1}{\\cos x}\\cdot \\dfrac{\\sin x}{\\cos x}\\,\\textrm d x.\n$$\n\nWe then use the fact that $\\dfrac{\\sin x }{\\cos x}  = \\tan x$ and $\\dfrac{1}{\\cos x} = \\sec x$ to express this as\n\n$$\n\\int_0^{\\pi/3} \\sec x\\tan x\\,\\textrm d x,\n$$\n\nwhich is a standard trigonometric integral. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡x{|}_{0}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})-\\operatorname{sec}⁡(0) \\\\  & =2-1 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/example-474.json" "file_sha256" "2cf8fdba454e5efb27b58c622b730f477ce82ca1ad68f95457734834988305c4"} {"question" "e-475" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int \\tan{2x}\\,\\textrm d x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/example-475.json" "file_sha256" "5e7ecb49eb8ea90acd2d7b3ccea5aa4987a0f40cd782d7721fbf5aa823b7c197"} {"question" "e-475" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We use the identity $\\tan 2x = \\dfrac{\\sin 2x}{\\cos 2x}$ and rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\tan{2x}\\,\\textrm d x = \\int \\dfrac{\\sin{2x}}{\\cos 2x}\\,\\textrm d x.\n$$\n\nNotice that the numerator of the integrand is proportional to the derivative of the denominator. So, we can solve this by substitution.\n\nLet $u=\\cos 2x.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}=-2 \\sin 2x \\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad -\\dfrac 1 2 \\,\\textrm d u= \\sin 2x \\, \\textrm d x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x|+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)^{-1}|+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{sec}⁡2x|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14036923/example-475.json" "file_sha256" "5e7ecb49eb8ea90acd2d7b3ccea5aa4987a0f40cd782d7721fbf5aa823b7c197"}] "usage" {"q-352868" [] "e-473" [] "e-475" [] "q-49070" [] "e-474" [] "q-49259" []} "basis" 1324 "retractions" [[17592186064762 :question/problem "What is $\\displaystyle \\int\\tan x(\\sec x + 2\\cos x)dx$?"] [17592186064772 :question/problem "What is $\\displaystyle \\int\\cot xdx$?"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186063084 17592186063085 17592186063086 17592186063087 17592186063143 17592186063144 17592186063145 17592186063146 17592186063147 17592186298554] "immutable_fields" [[17592186063083 :answer-field/correct] [17592186063083 :answer-field/id] [17592186063083 :answer-field/key] [17592186063083 :answer-field/type] [17592186063142 :answer-field/correct] [17592186063142 :answer-field/id] [17592186063142 :answer-field/key] [17592186063142 :answer-field/type